Model assets
------------

No model weights are stored in this repository. Poptart recognizes speech with
Parakeet from FluidInference and cleans transcripts with a Qwen 3.5 derivative
licensed Apache-2.0 (see Models/README.md). Both retain their upstream licenses
and notices when packaged into a Model Pack.


Managed recognition artifact attribution
----------------------------------------

Parakeet Unified English 0.6B is based on NVIDIA's Parakeet model; Core ML conversion
and Swift integration are by FluidInference. The artifact, unlike the FluidAudio
SDK, is CC-BY-4.0:
https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/parakeet-unified-en-0.6b-coreml/tree/4252711f6f060f9a2f91e5f081a806d7f45eebd8
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Poptart selects the upstream 70/7/1 int8 streaming encoder, decoder, joint-decision
bundle, vocabulary and metadata. These staged model files are unmodified.

Personal Vocabulary uses the Parakeet TDT-CTC 110M model developed by NVIDIA
and Suno, with Core ML conversion by FluidInference:
https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/parakeet-ctc-110m-coreml/tree/accdafd8cf8a2ff1cabe3c11e54416b405d409aa
https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt_ctc-110m
The original model and converted model-card metadata declare CC-BY-4.0.
The converted card's Apache-2.0 body statement conflicts with that metadata;
it is not evidence that NVIDIA's attribution terms have been removed.
Poptart stages the encoder, spectrogram and tokenizer files without changing
their bytes. Redistribution clarification remains part of release preparation.

Optional voice activity detection uses Silero VAD, copyright 2020-present
Silero Team, converted to Core ML by FluidInference, under the MIT License:
https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/silero-vad-coreml/tree/b419383c55c110e2c9271fa6ee0ea83d03c70d96
The selected bundle is silero-vad-unified-256ms-v6.2.1.mlmodelc, unmodified.
The full copyright and permission notice is in Models/notices/Silero-LICENSE.txt
and must accompany the VAD files in the distributed Model Pack.


